    "text": "As shown in figure below, a charge $+2 \\mathrm{C}$ is situated at the origin $O$ and another charge $+5 \\mathrm{C}$ is on the $x$ -axis at the point $A .$ The later charge from the point $A$ is then brought to a point $B$ on the $y$ -axis. The work done is $\\left(\\right.$ given $\\left.\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0}}=9 \\times 10^{9} \\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{F}\\right)$ <img src=\"assets\\qt0043_506810f3d981.png\">"
